---
import CaseLayout from '../../layouts/CaseLayout.astro';
import Intro from '../../components/case/Intro.astro';
import Meta from '../../components/case/Meta.astro';
import Stats from '../../components/case/Stats.astro';
import Chapter from '../../components/case/Chapter.astro';
import Figure from '../../components/case/Figure.astro';
import Quote from '../../components/case/Quote.astro';
import Lessons from '../../components/case/Lessons.astro';
import NextCase from '../../components/case/NextCase.astro';
import cover from '../../assets/moen/cover.png';
import beforeAfter from '../../assets/moen/before-after.png';
import flowMap from '../../assets/moen/flow-map.png';
import devices from '../../assets/moen/devices.png';
import screenWall from '../../assets/moen/screen-wall.png';
import foundations from '../../assets/moen/ds-foundations.png';
import components from '../../assets/moen/ds-components.png';
import sourceOfTruth from '../../assets/moen/source-of-truth.png';
import usability from '../../assets/moen/usability-test.png';
---

<CaseLayout
  title="Three apps, six devices, one Moen"
  description="Moen folded the apps of the companies it bought into one smart-water app. I was on the UX Cabin design system team and owned the source-of-truth file developers built from."
>
  <Intro
    title="Three apps, six devices, one Moen"
    tags={['Moen, via UX Cabin', 'iOS & Android · Design system', '2023']}
    lede="Moen moved into the smart home by buying companies, and each one came with its own app. Our team at UX Cabin folded them into one app for six water devices, built on a 400+ component system. I was on the system team. I kept every screen tied to the library and owned the source-of-truth file developers built from."
  >
    <Figure src={cover} alt="Screens from the merged Moen app on a slate background, showing home, water level, sensor trends and a sprinkler zone." eager />
  </Intro>

  <Meta
    rows={[
      ['Role', 'UI/UX designer, design system team'],
      ['Company', 'Moen, via UX Cabin'],
      ['Product', 'iOS & Android app, design system'],
      ['Period', '8 months, 2023'],
    ]}
  />

  <Stats
    items={[
      ['3 → 1', 'apps merged into one'],
      ['5', 'water devices on one home screen'],
      ['400+', 'components in the team’s library'],
    ]}
  />

  <Chapter title="One company, three apps">
    <p class="p">
      Moen bought two smart-water companies. Each came with its own app, its own navigation and its own idea of what a
      device was. A faucet, a sprinkler and a shutoff valve still needed their own controls, and a leak, an offline device
      or a failed pump had to read as urgent on every one of them.
    </p>
    <Figure src={beforeAfter} alt="Before, three apps, each with its own navigation. After, one app, one home screen for every device." />
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter title="Mapping what already existed">
    <p class="p">
      We put the old Sketch and Figma files on one board and mapped every screen to its flow. That map became the new
      information architecture.
    </p>
    <Figure
      src={flowMap}
      alt="One of many flows on the board, from the old sprinkler app. Home leads to Update Schedule (edit schedule on touch), which leads to Advanced; a long press on a zone opens Run time."
    />
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter title="Every device, one home screen">
    <p class="p">Every device opens from the same home screen and uses the same card, tabs and alert pattern.</p>
    <Figure
      src={devices}
      alt="The home screen’s devices row connects to five devices, each listing the components it reuses. The devices are the sprinkler controller, sump pump monitor, leak detector, Flo Shutoff and kitchen faucet."
    />
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter title="Screens from the whole app">
    <p class="p">
      Alerts, sprinkler zones, settings and device detail. Different products, built from the same cards, sheets and
      type.
    </p>
    <Figure src={screenWall} alt="A wall of Moen app screens, with zones, Flo Shutoff, device detail, smart leak detector, alerts and sprinkler controller." />
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter title="The system underneath">
    <p class="p">
      Atomic Design, built by the UX Cabin system team. I was on that team, and I made sure every component the screens
      needed existed, and that every screen used them correctly.
    </p>
    <Figure
      src={foundations}
      alt="Foundations. Eight colours and a nine-step grey ramp; an 8px grid annotated on the home screen with its exceptions; ten type styles on one scale; one icon set; every glyph fits a 16px box inside a 24px container."
    />
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter title="Every component, every state">
    <p class="p">
      Each module was documented with its states and a rule for when to use it, so screens were checked against the
      library, not against each other.
    </p>
    <Figure
      src={components}
      alt="Components. Primary and secondary buttons in four states; one device card for every device, with photo, title, status icons and actions; three levels of alert urgency."
    />
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter title="One source of truth">
    <p class="p">
      Four designers, six products, one Figma file. This part was mine. Screens attached to the library, missing
      components added, every flow annotated and linked before handoff.
    </p>
    <Figure
      src={sourceOfTruth}
      alt="The source-of-truth Figma file in Dev Mode, with every screen built from library instances, missing components raised and added, annotated and linked before handoff."
    />
  </Chapter>

  <Chapter title="Tested before it shipped">
    <p class="p">
      Complex flows, like setting a watering schedule, went through remote usability tests. Ratings, click paths and
      written answers went back into the designs.
    </p>
    <Figure
      src={usability}
      alt="Usability test of the watering schedule with 4 remote testers, 3:04 average time on task, none rated it difficult. One written answer said “We run ours in the early morning, around 5:30, before it can be too warm and any of it could evaporate.”"
    />
  </Chapter>

  <Quote
    quote="“We stood up a fully functional design system in a couple of months. Because of that we were able to get products out the door, period. Incredible ROI for us.”"
    by="Brian Colby, Principal UX Design, Moen"
  />

  <Lessons
    title="What it added up to"
    lede="Agency work at UX Cabin, alongside Moen’s in-house team. My part was system coverage, the source-of-truth file and the handoff."
    items={[
      ['Platform', 'Three apps shipped as one, with one navigation for every water device.'],
      ['The system', '400+ components, and every screen in the source file built from them.'],
      ['Handoff', 'Developers built from one file, with every flow annotated and linked to its prototype.'],
    ]}
  />

  <NextCase current="moen" />
</CaseLayout>
